doc_records.original_doc:
Creates and signs a JWT using the given algorithm.
@param algorithm The signing algorithm (e.g. HMAC256, RSA256)
@return The signed token as a compact serialized string
@throws SignatureGenerationException if signing fails

Verifies the signature and validates the claims of the given JWT.
@param token The compact serialized JWT string
@return The decoded JWT with verified claims
@throws JWTVerificationException if signature or claims validation fails

Decodes a JWT without verifying its signature.
@param token The compact serialized JWT string
@return The decoded JWT
@throws JWTDecodeException if the token is malformed

Adds a custom claim to the JWT payload.
@param name The claim name
@param value The claim value
@return This builder instance for chaining

Sets the expiration time (exp) claim.
@param expiresAt The expiration date
@return This builder instance for chaining

Signs this JWS object with the specified signer.
@param signer The JWS signer (e.g. RSASSASigner, MACSigner)
@throws JOSEException If the JWS object couldn't be signed

Verifies the signature of this JWS object.
@param verifier The JWS verifier (e.g. RSASSAVerifier, MACVerifier)
@return true if verified, false if signature check failed
@throws JOSEException If verification could not be performed

Encrypts this JWE object with the specified encrypter.
@param encrypter The JWE encrypter
@throws JOSEException If the JWE object couldn't be encrypted

Parses a JWT from its compact serialized form. The JWT type is determined by the header.
@param s The compact serialized JWT string
@return The parsed JWT (PlainJWT, SignedJWT, or EncryptedJWT)
@throws ParseException If the JWT could not be parsed

Attempts to authenticate the passed Authentication object.
@param authentication The authentication request object
@return A fully authenticated object including credentials
@throws AuthenticationException If authentication fails

Returns whether this filter chain is configured to handle the supplied request.
@param request The request to check
@return true if this chain is configured to handle the request

Encode the JWT claims set and sign the JWT.
@param parameters The JWT encoding parameters
@return The signed JWT

Allows restricting access based upon the HttpServletRequest using RequestMatcher implementations.
@param authorizeHttpRequestsCustomizer Customizer for authorization rules
@return The HttpSecurity for further configuration
